	// (ISO 32000-2 algorithm 2.B: at least 64 rounds of AES-128-CBC over 64
	// copies of password, K and user data, the next hash chosen by the sum of
	// the first 16 bytes mod 3, until the last byte is small enough).
	// The salt is dc[saltat, +8), the user data dc[uat, +ul). The first 32
	// bytes of the answer are left in `b`.
